# Wave E — ID Allocations Log (append-only)
#
# Purpose:
#   Prevent ID collisions between parallel sub-waves.
#   Each line is an atomic reservation, appended at publish time.
#
# Format (one reservation per line, fields separated by two spaces):
#   <ID_OR_RANGE>  <SCOPE>  reserved_by=<LANE>  at=<ISO8601_UTC>  [note=<short_text>]
#
# Rules:
#   - Append-only. Never edit or delete a prior line.
#   - A lane MUST reserve its Family IDs or atom ID ranges BEFORE publishing
#     proposal YAML that references them.
#   - Family IDs may be minted ONLY by Chat 1 / integration lead.
#   - Atom ranges MUST reference an already-minted Family ID.
#   - Interaction, OOS, and SRC IDs are allocated monotonically at publish
#     time and do NOT require reservation here unless a lane anticipates
#     heavy volume and wants to claim a range.
#
# Field reference:
#   <ID_OR_RANGE>  e.g. "F12", "F12  atoms 03-08", "OOS 010-015"
#   <SCOPE>        "family", "atoms", "oos", "src", "interactions"
#   <LANE>         "E1-Setup" (integration lead), "E1a_family_spine",
#                  "E1b_atoms", "E1c_authority_scope", "E1d_interactions",
#                  or a future lane label
#   <ISO8601_UTC>  e.g. "2026-04-17T00:56:00Z"
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
